WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.705 --> 00:00:07.438
Every key term and thinker in the course lives here, with real definitions and real citations.

2
00:00:07.438 --> 00:00:16.896
Search or browse by week. Terms are written in full sentences, enough to actually understand, and each carries the citation it comes from.

3
00:00:16.896 --> 00:00:27.899
Use terms to speak precisely. Ideas like the New Jim Code and intersectionality do exact work in this course. Written work reads stronger when the vocabulary is used accurately.

4
00:00:27.899 --> 00:00:38.723
Meet the scholars. Each week lists the scholars behind its readings, with a one-line version of what each argues. Click a name to open the source's detail page.

5
00:00:38.723 --> 00:00:45.953
Follow a term back to its week. Each entry names its home week, so you can revisit the fuller context.

6
00:00:45.953 --> 00:00:48.556
Nothing here is graded.

7
00:00:48.556 --> 00:00:53.121
Where next: Turn terms into memory with Concept Flashcards.
